{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. Thank you for being here. As you all know, the Department of Justice has issued a subpoena concerning commission payments made through our international distributors, and we need to provide an initial response and proposed investigation plan next month. Our current response packet describes the matter as an inquiry into distributor commissions, but it does not yet specify whether we will make a voluntary disclosure, a repayment amount, or an executive-interview protocol.

Before we can finalize anything, I need each of you — white-collar, finance, and employment counsel — to give me your final recommendation on every open response item. Once I've heard from all three of you, I'll record a definitive yes-or-no decision on voluntary disclosure and the other terms, along with implementation commitments. That's non-negotiable — this meeting doesn't end until those decisions are on the record.

So let's start with the basics. White-collar counsel, can you walk us through your recommendation on voluntary disclosure? Finance, I'll need your assessment of any repayment exposure. And employment counsel, I'll need your guidance on the executive-interview protocol. Let's get into it."}

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Before I give my recommendation, I want to put on the record a key scope issue I've identified. While reviewing the subpoena and its incorporated definitions, I confirmed that the requested commission records cover exactly four distributors during calendar years 2019 through 2021. I have not yet updated the response packet because my subpoena-scope memorandum is still in review. This is directly relevant to our disclosure and investigation-plan decisions, so I want everyone aware of it."}
```

